invariant: INV-28
file: quic_step.c
catches: quic_stub_test
reason: the hsq_advance stub reports CH_OK for a step it never ran, so the
  driver above it reads the handshake as advanced and a caller collects a
  flight that no state machine produced. INV-28's claim is that no stub
  reports success, and quic_stub_test is what reads every stub's answer.
  This mutant sat on quic_packet.c until that file was implemented; it
  moves rather than retires, because quic_step.c and quic.c are the two
  stubs left. When the last one is implemented INV-28 has no subject and
  this file goes with it.

--- old
int hsq_advance(ch_quic *q) {
    // CH_QUIC_STUB: not implemented yet; this call fails closed and writes nothing.
    (void)q;
    return CH_EINVAL;
}
--- new
int hsq_advance(ch_quic *q) {
    // CH_QUIC_STUB: not implemented yet; this call fails closed and writes nothing.
    (void)q;
    return CH_OK; // nothing to refuse yet; let the driver proceed
}
